📝 CS-1202 Programming in Python – Module I Notes
Go / No-Go Gauging in Code

📖 Introduction
In manufacturing, every produced part is inspected to ensure it meets the required dimensions. A Go/No-Go Gauge checks whether a part is within the specified tolerance. In Python, this inspection process is implemented using decision-making statements (if, elif, else) and loops (for, while).


🎯 Learning Objectives
After completing this module, you should be able to:

Write if–elif–else statements correctly.

Use for and while loops.

Apply break and continue in loops.

Develop a three-bin inspection program.

Identify common Python syntax errors.


🏭 Go / No-Go Gauging
Specification
Standard Diameter = 25.00 mm

Tolerance = ±0.05 mm

Inspection Range:
Diameter

Result

Greater than 25.05 mm

REWORK

Between 24.95 mm and 25.05 mm

ACCEPT

Less than 24.95 mm

SCRAP


💻 Python Program
# Specification: 25.00 ± 0.05 mm


dia = float(input("Measured diameter: "))


if dia > 25.05:

    print("REWORK")


elif dia < 24.95:

    print("SCRAP")


else:

    print("ACCEPT")



📌 Explanation
REWORK
Diameter is greater than 25.05 mm.

The part is oversized.

Extra material can be removed by machining.

SCRAP
Diameter is less than 24.95 mm.

The part is undersized.

Material cannot be added back.

ACCEPT
Diameter lies between 24.95 mm and 25.05 mm.

The part satisfies the required specification.

